cff-version: "1.2.0"
message: If you use this app, please cite it and the works it builds on, listed under references.
type: software
title: eeg-prep
abstract: The first step of the Pennsieve scalp EEG workflows. Reads clinical scalp EEG (BIDS-EEG, EDF/EDF+,
  BDF, BrainVision, EEGLAB, FIF, Nihon Kohden, Natus) with MNE-Python and MNE-BIDS, keeps the EEG channels
  under canonical 10-20 names with template positions, finds bad channels with pyprep (PREP), filters,
  re-references (average by default; bipolar-only recordings kept as pairs), removes eye, muscle and heart
  artifacts with ICA and ICLabel (mne-icalabel) and optionally ASR (python-meegkit), marks bad segments,
  reads seizure labels (BIDS/HED-SCORE events, EDF+ annotations, CHB-MIT summaries, labels.csv) and writes
  one BIDS-EEG derivative (EDF+) with a QC table and figures.
authors:
- name: Pennsieve (University of Pennsylvania)
contact:
- given-names: Joost
  family-names: Wagenaar
  orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0004-5925-5451
  affiliation: University of Pennsylvania
repository-code: https://github.com/pennsieve-apps/eeg-prep
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
- eeg
- scalp-eeg
- epilepsy
- electrophysiology
- bids
- preprocessing
- quality-control
- artifact-removal
- ica
- iclabel
